    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d804">

                <pb facs="0702" n="690" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.24/242: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-30T16:00:00+02:00">March 30, 1942—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:27 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>230. For Oscar Cox, General Counsel, Lend-Lease Administration, from
                        Kaufman.<anchor n="21" xml:id="d804-f1"/> The term lend-lease has apparently
                    never been understood <pb facs="0703" n="691" xml:id="pg691"/> by the Turks.
                    Since his arrival the Ambassador has explained to the Turkish authorities that
                    the Turkish Government is not required to pay the United States or the British
                    Government for the lend-lease material that is being shipped. It would therefore
                    be very helpful if a master lend-lease agreement with Turkey could be signed.
                    Such a document should make it clear just what the term lend-lease means in so
                    far as Turkey is concerned. The agreement could be negotiated at least in part
                    here if that is deemed desirable. [Kaufman.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d804-f1" n="21" xml:id="d804-f1-content">
                <p>Frank A. Kaufman, representative of the Lend-Lease Administration in Turkey.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
